# Pre-release for Obtainium after each feature

When a **user-facing** change is finished (chat, MQTT, UI, OS prompts, updates) — not a docs-only or rule-only tweak — ship a test APK the same session. Do not wait for a separate «зарелизь» unless they said not to release.

Obtainium reads **GitHub Releases**, not `dev` commits.

## Steps (always on `dev`, never `master`/`main`)

1. Commit the feature on `dev` if not already committed.
2. Bump in [app/build.gradle](app/build.gradle): `versionCode` +1; `versionName` next pre (`0.3.0-pre.2` → `0.3.0-pre.3`). Must be greater than the installed tag by `AppVersion`.
3. Commit the bump, `git push origin HEAD`.
4. Tag `v{versionName}` (example `v0.3.0-pre.3`), `git push origin v0.3.0-pre.3`.
5. CI on `v*` builds signed APK and a **prerelease**. Tell the user to wait for green Actions, then pull in Obtainium (Include prereleases). Both test phones need the same build for protocol changes.

## Skip

- User said not to tag / not to push.
- Only `.cursor/rules`, comments, or tests that do not change the APK.
- `master`/`main` still forbidden without an explicit «обнови master».
